BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 359.4 Tm (Explanation: Moving conducting blood through a magnetic field generates a voltage. The signal can be related to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 346.3 Tm (blood-flow velocity and hence flow under the meter's calibrated conditions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 330.2 Tm (Other options: Oxygen consumption, Korotkoff sounds and filtration are separate measurement concepts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 315.6 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0023 | CIRCULATION 1, p. 62) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 292.4 Tm (24. A resting adult has a blood pressure of 120/75 mmHg. Using the usual resting approximation, what is mean) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 278.7 Tm (arterial pressure?) Tj ET
