BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 654.5 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0025 | CIRCULATION 1, pp. 79-81) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 631.3 Tm (26. What helps maintain arterial blood flow during ventricular diastole, when the left ventricle is not) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 617.6 Tm (ejecting?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 600.9 Tm (Answer: B. Elastic recoil of arteries stretched during systole) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 584.6 Tm (Explanation: The aorta and large elastic arteries store energy during systole and release it as they recoil in) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 571.5 Tm (diastole, helping maintain downstream pressure and flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 555.4 Tm (Other options: Valve cusps prevent backflow but do not actively generate forward arterial pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 540.8 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0026 | CIRCULATION 1, pp. 56-57, 76-77) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 517.6 Tm (27. A deep vein in one leg becomes obstructed, increasing pressure in vessels upstream. What local change) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 503.9 Tm (most directly favours swelling?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 487.2 Tm (Answer: E. An increase in capillary hydrostatic pressure) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 470.9 Tm (Explanation: Impaired venous drainage raises capillary pressure and promotes movement of fluid from capillaries) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 457.8 Tm (into interstitial tissue.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 441.7 Tm (Other options: Higher plasma oncotic pressure or stronger lymphatic removal would oppose fluid accumulation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 427.1 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0027 | CIRCULATION 1, pp. 85-86, 90-93) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 403.9 Tm (28. A patient has very low plasma albumin but unchanged capillary blood pressure. Why can oedema develop?) Tj ET
