BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 370.9 Tm (Explanation: Albumin contributes strongly to plasma colloid osmotic pressure. Less albumin weakens the opposing) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 357.8 Tm (force to filtration, promoting net tissue fluid accumulation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 341.7 Tm (Other options: Low albumin affects oncotic pressure; it does not abolish hydrostatic pressure or convert lymph into plasma.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 327.1 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0028 | CIRCULATION 1, pp. 85-86, 90-93) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 303.9 Tm (29. A patient develops chronic swelling of an arm after axillary lymph nodes are removed. What is the main) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 290.2 Tm (reason?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 273.5 Tm (Answer: D. Interstitial fluid and proteins cannot drain normally through lymph vessels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 257.2 Tm (Explanation: Damage to lymphatic pathways reduces the return of interstitial fluid and proteins to the blood,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 244.1 Tm (producing lymphoedema.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 228.0 Tm (Other options: Lymphoedema is caused by impaired lymph removal, not complete loss of arterial flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 213.4 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0029 | CIRCULATION 1, pp. 60, 94-95; Regional, pp. 47-48) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 190.2 Tm (30. Why does walking help return blood from the leg veins to the heart?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 173.5 Tm (Answer: A. Muscle contractions compress veins while valves limit backward flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 157.2 Tm (Explanation: Contraction of leg muscles compresses nearby veins. One-way venous valves direct the displaced blood) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 144.1 Tm (centrally, limiting pooling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 128.0 Tm (Other options: Venous valves are passive one-way structures; muscle compression supplies the pumping action.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 113.4 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0030 | CIRCULATION 1, pp. 97-98) Tj ET
