BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 344.1 Tm (pressure difference / resistance\). The plateau reflects autoregulatory adjustment.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 328.0 Tm (Other options: Falling resistance alongside increasing pressure would increase, rather than stabilize, flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 313.4 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0034 | CIRCULATION 2, pp. 4-10) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 290.2 Tm (35. A person suddenly loses blood and arterial pressure falls. Which immediate autonomic change helps) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 276.5 Tm (restore pressure?) Tj ET
