BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 714.6 Tm (Answer: A. Increased arterial pressure with reflex slowing of the heart) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 698.3 Tm (Explanation: Reduced medullary perfusion causes a powerful sympathetic rise in systemic pressure. The resulting) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 685.2 Tm (arterial hypertension stimulates baroreceptors, producing reflex bradycardia.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 669.1 Tm (Other options: The raised pressure is a compensatory response to brainstem ischemia; bradycardia is secondary to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 656.5 Tm (baroreflex.) Tj ET
