BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 588.3 Tm (Answer: E. Through specific glucose transport proteins in the endothelial membrane) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 572.0 Tm (Explanation: The blood-brain barrier restricts paracellular movement, but glucose is carried across endothelial) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 558.9 Tm (membranes by transporters such as GLUT1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 542.8 Tm (Other options: Glucose does not normally pass freely between tightly joined endothelial cells.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 528.2 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0048 | Regional Circulation, pp. 18-20) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 505.0 Tm (49. Mean arterial pressure is 95 mmHg and intracranial pressure is 15 mmHg. Assuming cerebral venous) Tj ET
