BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 232.0 Tm (Explanation: The myocardium already extracts much of the oxygen from coronary blood at rest. Higher demand is met) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 218.9 Tm (largely by increased coronary flow, partly driven by metabolic vasodilators such as adenosine.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 202.8 Tm (Other options: Coronary metabolic regulation increases flow in active muscle; adenosine is a vasodilator in this setting.) Tj ET
